____________________________________________________________________________________________________
INTERMEDIATE STEADY STATE (absorbing barrier below the lowest threshold of each well)
____________________________________________________________________________________________________

J N = F with a lower absorbing barrier: the fate of the nascent, chemically activated adducts on their first
collisional descent (Gonzalez-Garcia, Olzmann, PCCP 12, 12290 (2010), Sec. 3.2; Olzmann, PCCP 4, 3614 (2002)).
A molecule transferred below the barrier counts as stabilized. Bimolecular rate coefficients k(R -> X) = k_inf Phi_X
(Pilling, Robertson, Annu. Rev. Phys. Chem. 54, 245 (2003), eq. 44).

